# promise: #754
# The space style editor's colour pad takes its first press while the page has the keys: a real press on the pad,
# through the window server (scripts/hid-click/click.m), dragged and let go, moves the colour, as Arc's does.
# Reported as the knob not grabbing until a click first (GitHub #754, part C): the editor is a non-activating panel
# beside the page, and its plain NSHostingView let that first press only make the panel key, so the pad's
# DragGesture never saw it. The editor's view takes the first mouse now (FirstClickHostingView).
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
pace 0.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=theme-pad
wait 2
cra://debug?mainFrame=100,100,1000,700
wait 1
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
# A real click on the page makes Cra the active app with the page holding the keys, as the reporter's was.
click page-top
wait 1
cra://debug?themeEditor=1
wait 1
# The browser window takes the keys back without a click (a click outside the editor closes it).
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
click theme-pad drag
expect-log theme pad key: no
expect-log theme editor pad dragged: key=#[0-9A-F]{6}
cra://dismiss
